{
  "v": 1,
  "about": [
    "Deck codes for server/pool/node/records/derive/deck.mjs (test/derive-deck.test.mjs) and the client's Cards/DeckString and DeckRecords.CardListKey (tests/Hearthpulse.Tests/OwnStats/DeckKeyAgreementTests.cs): TASK-2026-11-26-pro-collection B2, AC10.",
    "Real codes are copied from the repository files `made` names; the other codes are written byte by byte from a real list, as `made` says. Built 2026-11-26.",
    "key: the main deck as both readers read it, \"<dbf>x<copies>\" in dbf order (DeckRecords.CardListKey); null: a broken code both readers refuse.",
    "group: the cases of one group are one list; different groups are different lists.",
    "sideboard: the sideboard cards in the same form, \"\" without one, null when the code has one that does not read (SideboardUnread).",
    "canonical: the code deck.mjs encodeDeck and DeckString.Encode write for the list with the class and record format given.",
    "stricter: codes no game writes that the client still reads (client: its CardListKey, a minus sign written as '-') and the server refuses.",
    "heroes: class -> default hero (DeckString.ClassHero) and its dbf id in HearthstoneJSON enUS cards.collectible.json, read 2026-11-26.",
    "skins: hero dbf id -> card id and class of the hero skins the cases name, from HearthstoneJSON cards.json (ruRU, the app's cache of 2026-11-15). With heroes they give the class of every case's hero, which is the class of its canonical code."
  ],
